---
// Over the GPGPU video (Jason, 2026-10-22): says that the GPGPU on the board computes every step and the laptop only draws it,
// in short words on a narrow video, with pulses running along a copper trace from one to the other. Static under reduced motion.
---
<div class="onfpga"><div class="in">
  <span class="end">
    <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="5" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="#41e2f2" /><path d="M9 2v3M12 2v3M15 2v3M9 19v3M12 19v3M15 19v3M2 9h3M2 12h3M2 15h3M19 9h3M19 12h3M19 15h3" stroke="#d8b46a" stroke-width="1.5" /></svg>
    <span><b>32-core RISC-V GPGPU</b> <span class="l">on the FPGA computes every step</span><span class="s">A 32-core RISC-V GPGPU computes it</span></span>
  </span>
  <span class="wire" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i></span>
  <span class="end">
    <svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="13" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="#eaf2f1" stroke-width="1.6" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" stroke="#eaf2f1" stroke-width="1.6" /></svg>
    <span><b>The laptop</b> <span class="l">only draws them</span><span class="s">The laptop only draws it</span></span>
  </span>
</div></div>
